## PHASE 3: Output Format

Deliver in this fixed sequence.

---

### Page URL
`/[slug]`

---

### SEO Meta

**Title tag:** [60–65 characters. Primary keyword included. Written for clicks, not just ranking.]
**Meta description:** [150–160 characters. States what the page delivers and why to click.]
**Slug:** [kebab-case, keyword-first, no filler words]

---

### Page Copy

Output each section as a labeled block:

```
SECTION NAME

Headline: [section headline]
Subheadline: [if applicable]
Body: [section copy]
CTA Button: [button label, if applicable]
```

Tables (pricing, deliverables, comparisons) as Markdown tables within the section block.

Hero always includes: Headline + Subheadline + CTA Button.
Closing section always includes: CTA Button.

---

### JSON-LD Schema

Always generated. Always complete. Three required types inside a single `@graph`:

1. **LocalBusiness** (city-specific targeting) or **Organization** (national/international)
2. **Service** — one block per major service described on the page
3. **FAQPage** — one Question/Answer block per FAQ entry

For pricing ranges: `PriceSpecification` with `minPrice`, `maxPrice`, `priceCurrency`, `unitText`.
For fixed prices: `price` and `priceCurrency`.
For `areaServed`: named cities or countries from the brief — never "worldwide" as a placeholder.

Output as a valid `<script type="application/ld+json">` block.

---

### Image Alt Text

Four suggestions. Format: `[brand-slug]-[descriptor]-[location-or-context]`. Specific to page content. Keyword-relevant without being stuffed.

